From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:45:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: Sable Quick Settings header, Hub summary row and key
 hint
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Titan 2 shade artifact puts a "Sable Quick Settings" title card over
the compact row, a Hub summary row under it ("3 priority items · Enter
opens Hub") and a keyboard hint line; the locked shade shows the Hub
count only.

* SableShadeCoordinator counts Hub priority items on the list about to
  be rendered: heads-up, conversation and alerting notifications that
  are not ongoing (pure policy shade/sable/SableHubSummary). It reads no
  content; notifications hidden from the lock screen are not counted
  there. The count lives in SableShadeState (SysUISingleton).
* QSFragmentCompose, when config_sableShadeExtras is true, wraps the
  compact row with SableShadeHeader, SableHubSummaryRow and
  SableShadeKeyHint (measured into the QQS height, so notifications
  start below them) and adds the expanded hint under the tile grid.
* The Hub row is focusable with the QS focus ring; Enter or a tap opens
  Sable Start's Hub page (org.sableos.start.action.SHOW_HUB; the one
  Hub, as the Sable Hub app has no launcher entry) through
  ActivityStarter, which asks for unlock first on the lock screen. On
  a locked shade the row reads "N priority items · counts only". No row
  when Start cannot show its Hub page.
* The hint line shows only with a physical keyboard: "Alt+Down expand ·
  ↑↓ focus · Space toggle · Alt+Enter details" (Q25: Alt replaces Fn).

Defaults keep upstream; SableSystemUIOverlay turns it on.
